{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/3367-vigil-for-rome","id":3367,"title":"Vigil For Rome","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-05T04:57:24-08:00","id":3367,"title":"Vigil For Rome","content":"I proposed a Requiem For Rome game to my group, and their answer was that they love Rome but have no desire to play as vampires. They instead suggested we do a Hunter game set in the Roman Empire, which sounds fun as hell. The group has since split (thanks, college) but the idea has still stuck with me. Any idea how to go about doing this?<br /> <br /> Clearly, none of the modern Compacts and all but a few of the modern Conspiracies would be viable. We'd have the nascent Cainite Heresy and the Aegis Kai Doru running around (maybe the Ascending Ones as well? I'm terribly unfamiliar with them). I think the Vigil corebook mentions a compact of Roman Empire hunters (the Aves Minerva) but went into no detail on them.<br /> <br /> How would you guys do this game? What advice do you have? I think it would be a lot of fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T05:17:47-08:00","id":3378,"title":"","content":"I'd do a Tier 1 Rome game, at least to begin with. If you're throwing people into an unfamiliar setting like Ancient Rome, compact and conspiracies are going to make things more complicated to run.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T05:47:04-08:00","id":3397,"title":"","content":"The Aves Minverva can essentially be a proto-version of the Cainite Heresey, if you want. There's a more detailed write-up for them in the Paterfamilias SAS for RfR. So, with them and AKD you have a couple of conspiracies to start with. In the RfR corebook they describe members of the Mithraic Mysteries (many of whom were veteran soldiers) as potential antagonists, no reason you couldn't tweak something like the Malleus with a more pagan spin to fit that. A few years back I was also interested in doing a Roman Empire Vigil game and I came up with my own ancient tech-based conspiracy centered around Archimedes and his secret war against the undead. Basically he wrote up a codex of fighting techniques and contraptions which you could use all manner of sketchy historical evidence to allow things as various as flamethrowers, repeating crossbows and grenades into the mix. Call it Ancient Armory and use it the same way as TFV's Endowment and you're set.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/759-willr","name":"WillR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar759_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T06:23:11-08:00","id":3430,"title":"","content":"I didn't know there was more on the Aves Minerva; thanks for the heads up.<br /> <br /> I suppose the Knights of St. George would exist during this time, but without the pretense of being Anglican.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T07:36:55-08:00","id":5060,"title":"","content":"I'm loving the idea of an Aegis Kai Doru hunter coming from Greece to Rome and working alongside the Aves Minerva. Hundreds of years later, the same hunter (now immortal, a la the Crusader from Indiana Jones) running across the Cainite Heresy and being profoundly depressed by what has become of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T00:00:37-08:00","id":8641,"title":"","content":"I just ran a mortals w/1 mortal+ in an early Roman Empire era game Sunday using GMC update and my players loved it. They ended up fighting a minotaur/werebull at the palace of Knossis. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It was epic. Thanks for all these great ideas, the next time the my players play these PCs, they'll be part of a conspiracy!!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1031-youvegotwildtalents","name":"youvegotwildtalents","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T05:21:16-08:00","id":8736,"title":"","content":"If your game is set after the Roman Conquest of Egypt, the Ascending Ones (may be called the Cult of the Phoenix by then) could be included in your games.<br /> <br /> Cheiron group, under a different name, also could be included. There are archeological references linked to them since ancient Greece.<br /> <br /> There also could be some christian covenants, may be with no powers (as the Long Night, but different covenant), or even with the Benedictions (in the fluff it's said they're are pre-nicean). It could be interesting give them a change from current setting: the catholic/orthodox group could be a compact, without any magical power, and the gnostic group could be the one who uses the Benedictions (although without the saints reference and dates).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T13:25:55-08:00","id":10720,"title":"","content":"My Compact/Conspiracy list (they look like Compacts in terms of size, but have supernatural Endowments for their highest ranked members)<br /> <br /> Aegis Kai Doru, in Greece &amp; Asia Minor<br /> Aves Minerva, in Rome<br /> Bacchantes, cult of mad revelers and liberators<br /> Collegia Chironos, strange slave and freeman healers<br /> Cult of the Phoenix, in Egypt<br /> Fraternitas Amissa, guild of explorers, guides, and caravan guards<br /> Lux Mithrae, luminous warriors in the legions<br /> Noctis Vigiles, Pre-Nicean Christians with leaders afflicted with guiding visions<br /> Shoftim, &quot;judges&quot; who protect the dispersing Jews<br /> [Wunjo], Germanic pagan seekers of glory (their name is the literal rune, <a href=\"http://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/35/Runic_letter_wunjo.svg\" target=\"_blank\">http://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedi...tter_wunjo.svg</a>)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T13:57:59-08:00","id":10747,"title":"","content":"Lux Mithrae sound great. Any more on them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T14:02:21-08:00","id":10751,"title":"","content":"Have a look at <a href=\"http://forums.white-wolf.com/default.aspx?g=posts&amp;t=56809\" target=\"_blank\">this old thread</a> for more details <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> BTW Glamourweaver I noticed your Zoroasteran demon hunters are not on that list. Did you change your mind about them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T18:18:30-08:00","id":10958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/3367-vigil-for-rome?p=10751#post10751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have a look at <a href=\"http://forums.white-wolf.com/default.aspx?g=posts&amp;t=56809\" target=\"_blank\">this old thread</a> for more details <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> BTW Glamourweaver I noticed your Zoroasteran demon hunters are not on that list. Did you change your mind about them?</div> </div> </div> </div>The <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">An\u00fb\u0161iya exist, but I didn't list them because they don't have a presence in Roman territory. They're the (possibly related) counterpart to Lux Mithrae, fighting for Persia.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T18:31:36-08:00","id":10967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/3367-vigil-for-rome?p=10747#post10747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lux Mithrae sound great. Any more on them?</div> </div> </div> </div>They're basically the militarized hunter group, ala Task Force VALKYRIE, but with the highly ritualized uniting culture of Mithraism. Their Endowments involve sanctified bull blood used for rites to cause your sword or spear to glow with power, or even yourself for incredible physical feats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T08:03:08-08:00","id":11285,"title":"","content":"I would reverse engineer the Avis Minerva from them from these guys <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/585-covenant-the-athenic-church-the-women-of-war-and-wisdom\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...war-and-wisdom</a>.<br /> <br /> But Ascending Ones, Aegis Kai Doru and the Cheiron Group would be the major conspiracies I would use. I would also probably sneak in an appearance from the Lucifuge herself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":754,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","user":"Eldagusto","date":". 11-15-2013, 11:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T08:08:43-08:00","id":11289,"title":"","content":"Also I would use a proto version of these guys <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/561-conspiracy-hakollel-shel-hamerkava-the-secret-names-of-god\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...t-names-of-god</a>. Perhaps as the last group to have knowledge of Shemot, maybe divided between three secret families. I would probably also tie them in with relics such as one group having an egg from Moses' staff, another having some of Abel's blood, and the third having something like the first dry rock from after the flood that perhaps one of Noah's kids picked up. You could even run the fall of these three legacies, and Aves Minerva in game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T09:00:14-08:00","id":11320,"title":"","content":"I like those ideas for Relics, especially the dry rock (I imagine since Roman times they all got lost, destroyed, or found their way to the Ageis Kai Doru). I would definitely say there's Shemot wielders around the time Rome occupied Judea, those secrets weren't burred until after the Romans invaded.<br /> <br /> Whether they were monster hunters or just scholars and mystics is another question. Shemot were Glmaourweavers idea originally so maybe Shoftim have Shemot. Care to enlighten us Glmaourweaver <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/3367-vigil-for-rome?p=11285#post11285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would reverse engineer the Avis Minerva from them from these guys <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/585-covenant-the-athenic-church-the-women-of-war-and-wisdom\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...war-and-wisdom</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Aves Minerva are actually a cannon hunter group from the Roman era Vampire books so they're all written up already. They actually don't have any relationship to the Athenic Church (I knew they existed when I wrote the Athenic Church but none of the details) and a completely unrelated Endowment. They actually taught their Endowment to the Canite Heresy and thus form one of the biggest mysteries in Hunter:<br /> <br /> Why can a mostly agnostic group using Pagan magic see The Mark of Lucifuge (The Lucifuge can brand people with invisible marks: Only Lucifuge, MM and Canite hunters can see it). You have the two Christian Conspiracies and the Canites.<br /> <br /> There's also a mention somewhere that the leaders of the MM, the Lucifuge and an unnamed third person have secret meetings without their respective Conspiracies knowing. Something links those three groups.<br /> <br /> All this is getting off topic though <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> If you want to play with the Devotion endowment in Roman times may I recommend Isis? Partly because she has a <a href=\"http://isis.houseofneteru.com/names_of_isis.htm\" target=\"_blank\">ton of names and titles</a> but also because there's plenty of milage in Isis mystery cults around the time and the conflation between Isis and the Virgin Mary. Endowments based on leadership, metamagic and nature should be cool to work with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 11-16-2013, 08:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T09:28:50-08:00","id":11343,"title":"","content":"Around that time the Knights of St George operated, but as loners dedicated to the death of witches. And without their current cover with the church.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T17:39:18-08:00","id":11728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/3367-vigil-for-rome?p=11320#post11320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whether they were monster hunters or just scholars and mystics is another question. Shemot were Glmaourweavers idea originally so maybe Shoftim have Shemot. Care to enlighten us Glmaourweaver <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>They can of course, but that's not how I was imagining them. The Ma'asei Merkavah (my version of the Kabbalist Azoth-hunters) exist in the Roman Era, but aren't in the active hunting game yet - that won't happen till the Middle Ages. They're more insular mystics at this point. The Shoftim (Judges) are more martial and physical than that. I haven't decided on an appropriate Endowment for them yet, though I'm experimenting with a few ideas.<br /> <br /> As for the Lucifuge.... there is a moneyed woman, living in Rome called Lucilla - a widow she oversees the successful merchant house of her late husband. Rumors amongst hunters though claim that this has been the case on and off for centuries, with her moving away for a few years and then moving back under a different name and widow of a different man who bought the previous enterprise. She is known to hire hunters for certain jobs or just pass on useful information, but is also suspected of business dealings with less savory inhabitants of the city.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T00:56:57-08:00","id":15217,"title":"","content":"A Vigil for Rome game might finally be the thing to finally force me to use the Ascending Ones. They, the Aegis Kai Doru, and the Aves Minerva are probably the big Hunter muscle of the era, along with maybe some Mithras cultists in the legions. Having a few blessed Christians might be nice as well.<br /> <br /> What Endowment would the cult of Mithras have?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T01:35:10-08:00","id":15240,"title":"","content":"So beyond the Kindred of Rome, what monsters would Hunters be dealing with?<br /> <br /> Rome has a long history of shades, so ghosts are a given (though generally as neutral or prophetic forces), and I can vividly imagine some northern barbarians, thrown into frenzies and dressed in pelts, actually being werewolves. What Greek critters would you want running about? Because of Dark Eras, we know there were a large number of Mages in Greece (especially with Plato's stories of Atlantis, which he supposedly got from an Egyptian). I'm not familiar with Mummy; is there a Sothic Cycle any time during Rome (Republic or Empire)? There's a variety of options available, including some critters that didn't survive to the modern day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/memb